`(a, b) => ...` writes memory its caller can see at tests/wordings/nl2345_par_shared_write_reduce.ts:12:5, and `parallelReduce` runs it on several threads at once: a parallel body may read what its caller owns and write nothing but its result; make it answer what it computes and do the write after the call, or run it on the thread that called it, `let sum: i32 = 0; for (const b of src) { const a = sum; log.last = b; sum = a + b }`
